===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Physically [[secure]] and [[certain]], non-failing, reliable.
#: {{ux|en|This investment is a '''sure''' thing.}}
#: {{ux|en|The bailiff had a '''sure''' grip on the prisoner's arm.}}
#* {{RQ:Huxley Brave New World|passage='In the end,' said Mustapha Mond, 'the Controllers realized that force was no good. The slower but infinitely '''surer''' methods of ectogenesis, Neo-Pavlovian conditioning and hypnopædia…'}}
# Certain in one's [[knowledge]] or [[belief]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1827|author=w:Thomas De Quincey|title=On Murder Considered as one of the Fine Arts
|passage=The very excess of the extravagance, in fact, by suggesting to the reader continually the mere aeriality of the entire speculation, furnishes the '''surest''' means of disenchanting him from the horror which might else gather upon his feelings.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=IV|page=58|passage=The Celebrity, by arts unknown, induced Mrs. Judge Short and two other ladies to call at Mohair on a certain afternoon when Mr. Cooke was trying a trotter on the track. The three returned wondering and charmed with Mrs. Cooke; they were '''sure''' she had had no hand in the furnishing of that atrocious house.}}
#* '''2008 November 21''', Graham Linehan, ''{{w|The IT Crowd}}'', Season 3, Episode 1:
#*: ''Roy:'' I'm 95% '''sure''' it was him.<br>''Jen:'' You... you said you were 99% '''sure'''.<br>''Roy:'' I'm 97% '''sure''' it was him.
#: {{ux|en|Are you '''sure''' to succeed, as polls say? —Well, I am at least certain of making it to the podium this time.}}
#: {{ux|en|He was '''sure''' of being a finalist.}}
#: {{ux|en|They aren't '''sure''' who will attend [[for sure]].}}
#: {{ux|en|You seemed '''sure''' that the car was his.  Yeah. I’m not '''sure''' what is the point of spending hours and hours discussing this.}}
# {{lb|en|followed by a ''to'' infinitive}} Certain to act or be a specified way.
#: {{ux|en|Be '''sure''' to lock the door when you leave.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Adrian Spinelli|title=Listen: Star-studded Leonard Cohen tribute and a multimedia ode to Oakland's Black history|journal=w:San Francisco Chronicle|url=https://www.sfchronicle.com/entertainment/music/article/listen-star-studded-leonard-cohen-tribute-and-a-21173558.php|date=12 October 2022|passage=There’s nary a rock band as dynamic as the 1975 right now, and “Being Funny in a Foreign Language” is '''sure''' to be its fifth straight No. 1 album in the U.K. and perhaps even its second No. 1 in the U.S.}}
# Certain to obtain something.
#: {{ux|en|Many people book early [[in order to]] be '''sure''' of the best seats.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Free from danger; safe; secure.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Two Gentlemen of Verona|V|i|36|1|passage=Feare not: the Forreſt is not three leagues off, / If we recouer that, we are '''ſure''' enough.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Betrothed; engaged to marry.
#* '''c. 1513-1518''' (probably date written, published after '''1535''') {{w|Thomas More}}, ''History of King Richard III''
#*: The king was '''sure''' to Dame Elizabeth Lucy, and her husband before God.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1632|author=w:Richard Brome|title=w:The Northern Lass
|passage=I presum'd {{...}} [that] you had been '''sure''', as fast as faith could bind you, man and wife.}}

